<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MofonCode.Core" />
    <PackageReference Include="YamlDotNet" />
    <PackageReference Include="JsonSchema.Net" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- The scaffold a new solution starts from, embedded rather than written as string constants. The
       gate publishes single-file and a pre-tool hook invokes it on every tool call, so a template read
       from a path beside the binary is a template that is missing in exactly that case; a resource is
       inside the assembly. Named .template rather than .cs so nothing reads as source that is never
       compiled, and ScaffoldTests reads every one of them, which is what stops them rotting.

       WithCulture="false" is load-bearing, and the failure without it is a good trap. MSBuild infers a
       resource's culture from the second-to-last extension, and `cs` is the code for Czech - so
       `RepoFiles.cs.template` was taken for a Czech satellite of `RepoFiles.template` and went into a
       cs/ satellite assembly rather than the main one. Four templates embedded, seven vanished, and
       the only symptom was a scaffold that threw partway through writing files. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Init\Scaffold\*.template" WithCulture="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- The global constraint library, embedded for the same reason and with a sharper version of the
       same evidence: the packed tool shipped no library at all, so an installed gate could run `help`
       and `version` and nothing else, and both generated pipelines installed a binary whose one
       non-bypassable check could never pass. A resource cannot be left out of a package. The file
       beside the gate or above it still wins when there is one, which is what keeps editing
       CONSTRAINTS.md here from needing a rebuild. D-41. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="..\..\CONSTRAINTS.md" LogicalName="Sdlc.Core.CONSTRAINTS.md" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
